{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XtaoTu3VXQocpuvxACxWQC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context and determine what to build next.\n\n## Project Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is an experiment in specification-driven development using classic Unix utilities as a test bed. It derives formal specifications from C source code, generates Go implementations from those specs using an AI coding agent, and verifies parity against reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline: extract → specify → synthesize → verify. Key components:\n- `cmd/` - Go implementations of each utility\n- `pkg/testutils/` - Differential testing harness\n- `pkg/sys/` - Syscall abstractions (Darwin/Linux)\n\n\n- `pkg/format/` - Output formatting\n- `magefiles/` - Build targets\n- `docs/` - Specifications (PRDs, use cases, test suites)\n\n**Current State**: Specifications are mostly complete for the current roadmap, with rel01.0 (ts utility) having its PRD, use cases, and test suite finished but implementation still pending. The next releases—rel01.1 covering wc, cat, and sponge, rel02.0 with ls core and du, and rel02.1 with additional ls features—are all queued up.\n\n**Current Release**: rel01.0 focuses on the ts specification and differential testing. The use case rel01.0-uc001-ts is in progress with all spec artifacts complete. Looking at the dependency chain, pkg/testutils needs to come first since it's the differential testing harness that all utilities depend on, followed by cmd/ts which relies on it.\n\nSince I'm limited to one task, implementing pkg/testutils is the most impactful choice—it's the foundation blocking everything else. The implementation would span around 250-350 lines across files handling the DiffTest struct, binary execution, comparison logic, normalization hooks, and file-state comparison. `pkg/testutils/normalize.go` - TimestampNormalizer and normalizer composition\n- `pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go` - Unit tests\n\nThis should be around 250-350 lines. Let me draft the task.\n\nActually, looking at the PRD more carefully, the key requirements are: DiffTest struct with args, stdin, env, expected exit code, and normalization function; binary execution with timeout and working directory support; comparison and reporting with named subtests; composable normalizers including TimestampNormalizer; and file-state comparison for utilities like sponge. This is a reasonable single task to scope out.\n\nNow I need to check what exists in the project. Since the implementation_status shows everything is pending, I'll need to point the stitch agent to prd001-testutils.yaml for full requirements, go.mod for the module path, and the architecture docs for context. The agent will create difftest.go with the core DiffTest struct and execution logic, normalize.go for the normalizer implementations, and difftest_test.go for comprehensive unit tests.\n\nLooking at the scope, the production code should come in around 210 lines across the struct definitions, test execution, binary running with timeouts, output comparison with normalization, and file-state checking. Tests will add another 150 lines or so, which keeps this task appropriately sized.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74429,"cache_read_input_tokens":15594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74429},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1988ddfb-174b-41e2-b7c1-7e459a49b2e7","uuid":"cb5d1ff1-395a-4e12-bbf7-911ed1f70280"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XtaoTu3VXQocpuvxACxWQC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project Analysis\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven development experiment that re-implements Unix utilities in Go from C-source-derived specs, verified by differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) with shared components: `pkg/testutils` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format` (output formatting), and per-utility packages under `cmd/`.\n\n**Current State**: All specification artifacts (PRDs, use cases, test suites) are complete for rel01.0 through rel02.1. No implementation code exists yet -- all utilities are \"implementation pending.\"\n\n**Current Release**: rel01.0 (ts specification and differential test). The single use case `rel01.0-uc001-ts` is in_progress. The dependency chain is: `pkg/testutils` → `cmd/ts`.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe earliest incomplete release is rel01.0. `pkg/testutils` is the foundational component -- every utility's differential tests depend on it. It must be implemented before `cmd/ts` or any other utility. Per the dependency map, ts requires only `pkg/testutils` (no `pkg/sys` or `pkg/format`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74429,"cache_read_input_tokens":15594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74429},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1988ddfb-174b-41e2-b7c1-7e459a49b2e7","uuid":"c8282bd7-3cf4-4603-b9ab-ad199587cf2d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XtaoTu3VXQocpuvxACxWQC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BjbD4gT7i8UQQLWWJZyUGD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/petardjukic/WORKSPACE/go-unix-utils/.cobbler/measure-20260223-220750.yaml","content":"- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/testutils differential testing harness\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (full PRD with all requirements R1-R5 and acceptance criteria)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (components section -- understand how pkg/testutils fits as the shared verification layer)\n      - go.mod (module path and Go version)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.0.yaml (test suite for ts -- shows how TimestampNormalizer is used in practice)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct, Normalize type, RunDiffTests entry point, binary execution, comparison and reporting logic\n      - path: pkg/testutils/normalize.go\n        action: create\n        note: TimestampNormalizer, ComposeNormalizers helper, and any shared normalization utilities\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for RunDiffTests, normalization, file-state comparison, and timeout behavior\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: >\n          Define a DiffTest struct in pkg/testutils with fields: Name (string, used as subtest name),\n          Args ([]string), Stdin ([]byte, nil means no stdin/immediate EOF), Env ([]string, nil means\n          inherit test process environment), ExitCode (int, expected exit code), Normalize ([]NormalizeFunc\n          where NormalizeFunc is func([]byte) []byte -- applied in order; nil or empty means no normalization),\n          ExpectedFile (optional *FileExpectation struct with Path string and Content []byte for utilities\n          whose output is a file rather than stdout), and WorkDir (string, optional working directory --\n          empty means use a per-test temp directory created by the harness).\n      - id: R2\n        text: >\n          Implement a RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary string, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) function.\n          For each DiffTest, call t.Run(test.Name, ...) to create a named subtest. Within each subtest:\n          (a) create a temp directory if WorkDir is empty, (b) execute both binaries with identical args, stdin,\n          env, and working directory, (c) capture stdout, stderr, and exit code from each, (d) apply the\n          Normalize functions in order to both stdouts and both stderrs, (e) compare normalized stdout\n          byte-for-byte, normalized stderr byte-for-byte, and exit codes exactly, (f) if ExpectedFile is\n          non-nil, read the file at ExpectedFile.Path relative to the working directory after each binary\n          exits and compare content byte-for-byte.\n      - id: R3\n        text: >\n          Implement binary execution with a configurable timeout. The default timeout is 10 seconds.\n          Use exec.CommandContext with context.WithTimeout. If either binary exceeds the timeout, fail the\n          test with a clear message indicating which binary timed out. Capture stdout and stderr into\n          separate bytes.Buffer instances. Extract the exit code from the *exec.ExitError (or 0 if err is\n          nil). Do not write any output to the test process stdout or stderr during a passing test.\n      - id: R4\n        text: >\n          On comparison failure, report all of: the DiffTest args, stdin content (truncated to 256 bytes\n          if longer), reference binary stdout, Go binary stdout, reference binary stderr, Go binary stderr,\n          reference exit code, and Go exit code. Use t.Errorf with a formatted message that includes all\n          these fields. The message must clearly label each field (e.g., \"Args:\", \"Ref stdout:\", \"Go stdout:\").\n      - id: R5\n        text: >\n          Implement a TimestampNormalizer (a NormalizeFunc) that replaces common timestamp patterns with\n          the fixed string \"TIMESTAMP\". The patterns to match are: (a) syslog/default ts format matching\n          the regex for \"Mon DD HH:MM:SS\" (e.g., \"Feb 19 14:05:32\"), (b) ISO-8601 datetime\n          \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS\" with optional fractional seconds and timezone, (c) elapsed time format\n          \"HH:MM:SS\" at the start of a line (for ts -s and -i modes). Use regexp.ReplaceAll for each\n          pattern. The normalizer is used by cmd/ts differential tests.\n      - id: R6\n        text: >\n          Implement a ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc function that returns a single\n          NormalizeFunc applying each function in order. This is a convenience for building normalizer\n          chains.\n      - id: R7\n        text: >\n          For file-state comparison (R2 step f): when ExpectedFile is set, after each binary executes,\n          read the file at the given path. Compare the two file contents byte-for-byte. Report divergence\n          in the same format as stdout divergence (showing both file contents and the path).\n      - id: R8\n        text: >\n          Write unit tests in difftest_test.go that verify: (a) RunDiffTests passes when two identical\n          binaries (use /bin/echo or a simple Go test helper binary) produce the same output, (b)\n          RunDiffTests fails (using a testing helper that expects failure) when outputs differ, (c)\n          TimestampNormalizer replaces \"Feb 19 14:05:32\" with \"TIMESTAMP\", (d) TimestampNormalizer\n          replaces \"00:00:05\" at line start with \"TIMESTAMP\" (elapsed mode), (e) ComposeNormalizers\n          applies functions in order, (f) a test with a timeout shorter than the binary runtime\n          produces a timeout failure. For tests that need a binary, build a small Go program in a\n          TestMain or use /bin/echo and /bin/cat which are available on all Unix systems.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: >\n          Use testing.T as the only test framework. Do not import testify or other assertion libraries.\n          The project uses only the Go standard library plus golang.org/x/sys.\n      - id: D2\n        text: >\n          The module path is github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils. Package import path will be\n          github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils.\n      - id: D3\n        text: >\n          NormalizeFunc is defined as a named type: type NormalizeFunc func([]byte) []byte. The DiffTest\n          Normalize field is []NormalizeFunc (a slice, not a single function) so normalizers compose\n          naturally without a separate wrapper. ComposeNormalizers is a convenience but the slice is\n          the primary mechanism.\n      - id: D4\n        text: >\n          Exit code extraction pattern: when exec.Command returns a non-nil error, type-assert to\n          *exec.ExitError and call ExitCode(). When err is nil, the exit code is 0. When err is non-nil\n          but not an *exec.ExitError (e.g., binary not found), fail the test with the error message.\n      - id: D5\n        text: >\n          The FileExpectation struct enables sponge-style tests where the utility writes to a file\n          instead of stdout. The harness reads the file after execution and compares. This avoids\n          requiring each cmd/ test to implement its own file comparison.\n      - id: D6\n        text: >\n          All regexp patterns for TimestampNormalizer should be compiled once at package level using\n          regexp.MustCompile, not inside the function body, to avoid repeated compilation.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: >\n          pkg/testutils compiles with no errors: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/...\" succeeds.\n      - id: AC2\n        text: >\n          go vet ./pkg/testutils/... produces no warnings.\n      - id: AC3\n        text: >\n          go test ./pkg/testutils/... passes with all tests green.\n      - id: AC4\n        text: >\n          RunDiffTests correctly passes when both binaries produce identical output (verified by test).\n      - id: AC5\n        text: >\n          RunDiffTests correctly reports failure when outputs differ (verified by test using\n          testing.T helper or by checking test output).\n      - id: AC6\n        text: >\n          TimestampNormalizer replaces syslog-format timestamps (\"Feb 19 14:05:32\") with \"TIMESTAMP\"\n          (verified by unit test).\n      - id: AC7\n        text: >\n          TimestampNormalizer replaces elapsed-time timestamps (\"00:00:05\" at line start) with\n          \"TIMESTAMP\" (verified by unit test).\n      - id: AC8\n        text: >\n          A DiffTest with timeout shorter than binary runtime fails with a timeout message\n          (verified by unit test using sleep or a slow command).\n      - id: AC9\n        text: >\n          Production code (difftest.go + normalize.go) is between 200 and 350 lines.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74429,"cache_read_input_tokens":15594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74429},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1988ddfb-174b-41e2-b7c1-7e459a49b2e7","uuid":"330d546a-5827-470b-9a60-d98ac2128500"}
